w(389,"Tested live in the browser pane by hand. A clothing job (a panjabi) went through every step on the real screens: price sent by the owner, checked and confirmed by the buyer, advance received, craftsman given the job, work started. Then the owner pressed Call for a trial and, after it, Trial finished.",
 ["The owner's steps for clothing include Call for a trial next to It is ready; the job moved to the state trial",
  "The buyer's job page changed to \"Ready for a trial\" and the history says \"Ready for a trial.\" with the time",
  "The owner's job then offered Trial finished and It is ready; Trial finished put the job back to being made, so the fitting is a step between making and ready",
  "Starting work was refused until a craftsman had been given the job (\"Give the job to a craftsman before the work starts\")"],
 [{"file":"f389_1.jpg","caption":"Owner: the job in trial with Trial finished and It is ready","role":"admin","url":"/admin/custom"},
  {"file":"f389_2.jpg","caption":"Buyer: the job page during the trial","role":"buyer","url":"/custom/..."}],
 ["Done by hand in the live browser. The trial step is for clothing only (wood has no such button). The message to the buyer says Ready for a trial but does not give a time or place; that is left to the chat."])
